      "id": "2066972639801770317",
      "text": "A growth hacker on Twitter shared a breakdown of how Claude Fable 5 one-shotted a slick landing page with Three.js animations, claiming anyone could spin up an autonomous digital product business over the weekend for twenty dollars in API tokens.\n\nThe timeline thought that was the story. It was not.\n\nThe real shift wasn't a solo founder skipping an agency retainer. It was an enterprise web infrastructure engineer using a disposable developer identity to pull the verified UI component library and Stripe endpoints directly into a self-testing environment, bypassing the entire front-end engineering organization and internal QA gatekeepers without an employee ID.\n\nThe infrastructure required to run this operates at absolute margin. Anthropic charges ten dollars per million input tokens for Fable 5, and with prompt caching slashing that cost by ninety percent, a multi-turn autonomous coding loop that fixes its own bugs costs less than a coffee to generate production-ready code.\n\nPolymarket gives 78% odds that Anthropic IPO by December 31, 2026. That consensus is exactly why the bypass works unnoticed, as the market prices the company on traditional corporate expansion timelines while a single engineer can silently strip the labor cost out of enterprise deployment.\n\nhttps://t.co/aeY02tBJz4",
